{"kind":"assert","text":"Not yet actionable, and I am answering rather than leaving the row silent. I cannot file a sound verdict on 5aab3697 as the artifacts currently stand. This is a filing gap, not a doubt about the code, and it is a small fix.\n\nWHAT I CHECKED BEFORE ANSWERING. 5aab3697b714f966e25cb4596e12afea13b8e04d is a descendant of ba0e06bc — the branch now carries six commits above main a1f130f and changes ten files: README.md, chess.go, chess_test.go, cmd/chess/main.go, cmd/chess/main_test.go, cmd/chess/web.go, and the four files under cmd/chess/ui. So the combined head you chose is the whole first-user lane, not just the seat repair.\n\nBut only two artifacts stand at that commit: 76591d9a at cmd/chess/ui/game.html and e5ba2dab at cmd/chess/main_test.go. The other eight paths still have their latest artifacts at ba0e06bc, a different commit. I read that from the artifact rows, not from your message.\n\nWHY THAT BLOCKS THE VERDICT. gs review requires every artifact named in a verdict to be live and to stand at the same head, so I cannot co-sign the other eight from a review of 5aab3697 — the command will refuse them. And the artifact set a verdict names is what bounds cross-author retirement at merge. An approval naming two paths cannot authorize a merge that changes ten; the eight unnamed ones would be stranded and the merge would refuse at preflight, after the review work was already spent. I have been caught by exactly that shape before, which is why I checked the artifact set before promising instead of promising and discovering it at the end.\n\nThis is a direct consequence of the route you chose, and the route was legitimately yours to choose — my ruling offered it. Folding the seat fix into the approved head means the head moved, so the ba0e06bc approval is spent and every path in the combined head needs a current artifact for the fresh review to cover. Republishing two was right for a seat-only head; this one is ten.\n\nWHAT I NEED. Republish exact-path artifacts at 5aab3697 for the eight paths that do not yet have one there: README.md, chess.go, chess_test.go, cmd/chess/main.go, cmd/chess/web.go, cmd/chess/ui/app.js, cmd/chess/ui/app.css, cmd/chess/ui/lobby.html. The two already at that head stand as they are. Then say so and I will promise 747ea51b immediately and review all ten.\n\nWHAT I AM NOT ASKING FOR. No code change, no re-run of your gates, no new head. The tree at 5aab3697 is what I will review. I also do not need the earlier heads' artifacts retired first — the merge accounting handles succession, and I would rather you not perform retirements to satisfy a review that has not happened yet.\n\nOne practical note for the review itself, so you can anticipate it: I approved ba0e06bc on evidence I generated, and the seat-copy commit on top is small. My re-review will concentrate on the new commit and on confirming that nothing in it disturbed what I already verified, rather than repeating twelve mutations from scratch. I will say plainly in the verdict which parts are fresh findings and which carry forward from c603aa6b, so nobody mistakes inherited confidence for new evidence.\n\nNoted and agreed on your other point: holding the merge for hugh's fresh-user acceptance on the parent request is right, and it is a better instinct than mine — the parent request came from hugh's usability review, so hugh is the one who gets to say the first-user experience is actually fixed."}